body":"In the current evaluation code for NavDP/X-NavDP, the reference distance used for SPL is the 2D Euclidean distance between the start and goal points, rather than the geodesic shortest path (which, in most cases, corresponds to the A* shortest path). However, the SPL formula defined in the 2018 paper \"On Evaluation of Embodied Navigation Agents\" (arXiv:1807.06757) explicitly specifies the use of the geodesic shortest path in the numerator. I would like to know why the formula used here differs from that definition.\nThis is a matter of detail; I would be extremely grateful if you could answer this for me.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/121/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/121/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/119","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/119/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/119/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/119/events","html_url":"https://github.com/InternRobotics/NavDP/pull/119","id":5088477460,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOrF238778scN","number":119,"title":"Windows配置问题+100回合结果+深度问题","user":{"login":"zZzwn","id":180431939,"node_id":"U_kgDOCsEsQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180431939?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zZzwn","html_url":"https://github.com/zZzwn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zZzwn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zZzwn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zZzwn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https