,"id":147295651,"node_id":"U_kgDOCMeNow","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/147295651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study","html_url":"https://github.com/Slias-study","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Slias-study/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-31T06:39:26Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T06:39:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hello, when I used the provided navdp-cross-modal.ckpt to evaluate in the easy scenes with eval_imagegoal_wheeled.py, I found that the success rate was only around 30%. The evaluation results for the easy_2 scene are shown below (31%)  is far from the data normally reported in the paper, and I'm really puzzled about what went wrong.\n\nhttps://pan.baidu.com/s/18xpCIo9pvXCGiJanK8zzuQ?pwd=8e59","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/118/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/118/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/112","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/112/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/112/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/112/events","html_url":"https://github.com/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/112","id":4463983793,"node_id":"I_kwDOOrF2388AAAABChL8sQ","number":112,"title":"Clarification: does the LogoPlanner startgoal Isaac simulation evaluation use simulator GT pose for MPC tracking?","user":{"login":"mhqin1018","id":35513276,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTEzMjc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35513276?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018","html_url":"https://github.com/mhqin1018","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mhqin1018/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-17T15:36:36Z","updated_at":"2026-05-17T15:36:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"  Hi, thanks for releasing LoGoPlanner and the NavDP benchmark.\n\n  I want to clarify the simulation evaluation protocol. The paper/project page describes LoGoPlanner as using implicit localization without an\n  external localization/odometry module. From the released code, I agree that the LoGoPlanner policy/server itself does not seem to take GT pose\n  as input.\n\n  ## Policy/server side\n\n  `logoplanner_server.py` only receives goal/RGB/depth and returns trajectories:\n\n  ```python\n  goal_data = json.loads(request.form.get('goal_data'))\n  image_file = request.files['image']\n  depth_file = request.files['depth']\n\n  execute_trajectory, all_trajectory, all_values, trajectory_mask, sub_pointgoal_pd = \\\n      logoplanner_navigator.step_pointgoal(goal, image, depth)\n\n  return jsonify({\n      'trajectory': execute_trajectory.tolist(),\n      'all_trajectory': all_trajectory.tolist(),\n      'all_values': all_values.tolist(),\n      'sub_pointgoal_pd': sub_pointgoal_pd.tolist()\n  })\n```\n\n  ## Isaac simulation evaluator side\n\n  In `eval_startgoal_wheeled.py`, the low-level MPC tracker appears to use simulator GT pose as feedback. x0 is built from Isaac camera/root state:\n  ```python\n  camera_pos = env.unwrapped.scene.sensors['camera_sensor'].data.pos_w.cpu().numpy()\n  camera_rot_quat = env.unwrapped.scene.sensors['camera_sensor'].data.quat_w_world.cpu().numpy()\n  camera_rot = R.from_quat(camera_rot_quat[:, [1, 2, 3, 0]]).as_matrix()\n\n  robot_vel = env.unwrapped.scene.articulations['robot'].data.root_lin_vel_w[0, :2].norm().cpu().numpy()\n  robot_ang_vel = env.unwrapped.scene.articulations['robot'].data.root_ang_vel_w[0, 2].cpu().numpy()\n\n  x0 = np.stack([\n      camera_pos[:, 0],\n      camera_pos[:, 1],\n      np.arctan2(camera_rot[:, 1, 0], camera_rot[:, 0, 0]),\n      [robot_vel],\n      [robot_ang_vel],\n  ], axis=-1)\n```\n\n  Then this state is passed to MPC:\n  ```python\n  opt_u_controls, opt_x_states = mpc.solve(x0[i, :3])\n  ```\n  And tracking_utils.py sets it as the MPC initial state:\n  ```python\n  self.opti.set_value(self.opt_x0, x00)\n  ```\n  ## My understanding\n\n  1. LoGoPlanner policy/server does not use GT pose as input.\n  2. The released Isaac simulation evaluator does use simulator GT pose for low-level MPC tracking.\n  3. This GT feedback may correct tracking/odometry errors during simulation, even though it is not part of the policy input.\n\n  Could you clarify whether the reported simulation results use this GT-pose MPC feedback？\n  Thanks.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/112/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/112/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/111","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/111/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/111/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/InternRobotics/NavDP/issues/111/events","html_url":"https://github.com/InternRobotics/NavDP/pull/111","id":4404648526,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOrF2387ZcMtl","number":111,"title":"添加 LabUtopia-navigation 子模块和 test_yaml_data 测试数据","user":{"login":"buyaoxiangtale","id":146983769,"node_id":"U_kgDOCMLLWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146983769?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/buyaoxiangtale","html_url":"https://github.com/buyaoxiangtale","followers_url":"https://api.